        "original_id": "c81a286e-461c-5b4e-896d-f512f3636e31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Victor Garber, Teri Copley\n- TV Series: I Had Three Wives, We Got It Made, Alias\n- Films and Stage Works: Godspell, Assassins, Lend Me a Tenor, Titanic, Argo\n- Roles: Jesus, Anthony Hope, John Wilkes Booth, Jack Bristow, Max, Thomas Andrews, Ken Taylor\n\nFacts:\n- In 1983, Teri Copley was known for a role on the American NBC/syndicated television series \"We Got It Made,\" which premiered that year.\n- In 1985, Teri Copley subsequently co-starred on the CBS television series \"I Had Three Wives.\"\n- Victor Garber was the lead of \"I Had Three Wives,\" and the series was his first starring role on television.\n- Victor Garber is known for playing Jesus in \"Godspell,\" John Wilkes Booth in \"Assassins,\" Jack Bristow in the television series \"Alias,\" Max in \"Lend Me a Tenor,\" Thomas Andrews in James Cameron's \"Titanic,\" and Ken Taylor, the Canadian Ambassador to Iran, in \"Argo.\"\n- The chunk also states that Victor Garber is known for playing Anthony Hope in an unspecified work.",
